{"page":157,"blocks":[{"x":0.7305,"y":0.05257,"w":0.22101,"h":0.01535,"fs":0.01535,"n":2,"k":1,"t":"3.3 Differentiation Rules 143"},{"x":0.50365,"y":0.08769,"w":0.13373,"h":0.0371,"fs":0.01918,"n":1,"k":0,"t":"exb = ex # 0 - 1 # ex"},{"x":0.36258,"y":0.09472,"w":0.1512,"h":0.03052,"fs":0.01279,"n":5,"k":0,"t":"(b) d dx (e-x) = d dx a 1"},{"x":0.57981,"y":0.09744,"w":0.10153,"h":0.0294,"fs":0.01279,"n":2,"k":0,"t":"(ex)2 = -1"},{"x":0.66557,"y":0.10328,"w":0.07307,"h":0.02151,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"ex = -e-x"},{"x":0.36258,"y":0.14369,"w":0.26871,"h":0.01311,"fs":0.01311,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"Proof of the Derivative Quotient Rule"},{"x":0.62753,"y":0.16741,"w":0.11038,"h":0.03008,"fs":0.01279,"n":2,"k":0,"t":"u(x + h) y(x + h) - u(x)"},{"x":0.71137,"y":0.18394,"w":0.0268,"h":0.01347,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"y(x)"},{"x":0.52413,"y":0.18488,"w":0.03859,"h":0.0305,"fs":0.01279,"n":2,"k":1,"t":"d dx au"},{"x":0.55428,"y":0.18488,"w":0.06676,"h":0.02664,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"yb = lim"},{"x":0.59793,"y":0.20507,"w":0.02453,"h":0.01039,"fs":0.00895,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"hS0"},{"x":0.62467,"y":0.22279,"w":0.19556,"h":0.01347,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":0,"t":"y(x)u(x + h) - u(x)y(x + h)"},{"x":0.58093,"y":0.23211,"w":0.04011,"h":0.01347,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"= lim"},{"x":0.6753,"y":0.2394,"w":0.09429,"h":0.01347,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"hy(x + h)y(x)"},{"x":0.59793,"y":0.24254,"w":0.02453,"h":0.01039,"fs":0.00895,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"hS0"},{"x":0.36257,"y":0.26349,"w":0.59308,"h":0.02814,"fs":0.01279,"n":2,"k":1,"t":"To change the last fraction into an equivalent one that contains the difference quotients for the derivatives of u and y, we subtract and add y(x)u(x) in the numerator. We then get"},{"x":0.44669,"y":0.29819,"w":0.03859,"h":0.0305,"fs":0.01279,"n":2,"k":1,"t":"d dx au"},{"x":0.47685,"y":0.29819,"w":0.06676,"h":0.02664,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"yb = lim"},{"x":0.54723,"y":0.29863,"w":0.35044,"h":0.01347,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":0,"t":"y(x)u(x + h) - y(x)u(x) + y(x)u(x) - u(x)y(x + h)"},{"x":0.6753,"y":0.31524,"w":0.09429,"h":0.01347,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"hy(x + h)y(x)"},{"x":0.52049,"y":0.31838,"w":0.02453,"h":0.01039,"fs":0.00895,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"hS0"},{"x":0.55001,"y":0.33508,"w":0.1384,"h":0.0228,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":0,"t":"y(x)u(x + h) - u(x)"},{"x":0.62962,"y":0.33508,"w":0.22217,"h":0.03007,"fs":0.01279,"n":2,"k":0,"t":"h - u(x)y(x + h) - y(x)"},{"x":0.50349,"y":0.3623,"w":0.04011,"h":0.01347,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"= lim"},{"x":0.65788,"y":0.36299,"w":0.20258,"h":0.02174,"fs":0.01279,"n":2,"k":1,"t":"y(x + h)y(x) ."},{"x":0.52049,"y":0.37273,"w":0.02453,"h":0.01039,"fs":0.00895,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"hS0"},{"x":0.36257,"y":0.39368,"w":0.59303,"h":0.02814,"fs":0.01279,"n":2,"k":1,"t":"Taking the limits in the numerator and denominator now gives the Quotient Rule. Exercise 74 outlines another proof."},{"x":0.36258,"y":0.43844,"w":0.58901,"h":0.02814,"fs":0.01279,"n":2,"k":1,"t":"The choice of which rules to use in solving a differentiation problem can make a dif- ference in how much work you have to do. Here is an example."},{"x":0.36258,"y":0.48278,"w":0.26156,"h":0.01449,"fs":0.01407,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"EXAMPLE 9 Find the derivative of"},{"x":0.58135,"y":0.4998,"w":0.14612,"h":0.02727,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":0,"t":"y = (x - 1)(x2 - 2x)"},{"x":0.66365,"y":0.51428,"w":0.06962,"h":0.02167,"fs":0.01279,"n":2,"k":1,"t":"x4 ."},{"x":0.36258,"y":0.54028,"w":0.59305,"h":0.04434,"fs":0.01279,"n":4,"k":1,"t":"Solution Using the Quotient Rule here will result in a complicated expression with many terms. Instead, use some algebra to simplify the expression. First expand the numer- ator and divide by x4:"},{"x":0.44492,"y":0.58715,"w":0.14612,"h":0.02727,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":0,"t":"y = (x - 1)(x2 - 2x)"},{"x":0.52722,"y":0.58927,"w":0.18701,"h":0.03403,"fs":0.01279,"n":2,"k":0,"t":"x4 = x3 - 3x2 + 2x"},{"x":0.65828,"y":0.59647,"w":0.21143,"h":0.02683,"fs":0.01279,"n":2,"k":0,"t":"x4 = x-1 - 3x-2 + 2x-3."},{"x":0.36259,"y":0.63233,"w":0.23678,"h":0.01279,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"Then use the Sum and Power Rules:"},{"x":0.55161,"y":0.65245,"w":0.23711,"h":0.02973,"fs":0.01279,"n":2,"k":0,"t":"dy dx = -x-2 - 3(-2)x-3 + 2(-3)x-4"},{"x":0.60488,"y":0.68818,"w":0.04839,"h":0.02887,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":0,"t":"x2 + 6"},{"x":0.64259,"y":0.68818,"w":0.04839,"h":0.02879,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":0,"t":"x3 - 6"},{"x":0.57445,"y":0.68834,"w":0.04112,"h":0.01982,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"= - 1"},{"x":0.68029,"y":0.69538,"w":0.01899,"h":0.02167,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"x4."},{"x":0.36258,"y":0.7321,"w":0.28802,"h":0.01375,"fs":0.01375,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"Second- and Higher-Order Derivatives"},{"x":0.36258,"y":0.75608,"w":0.59301,"h":0.05951,"fs":0.01279,"n":4,"k":1,"t":"If y = ƒ(x) is a differentiable function, then its derivative ƒ′(x) is also a function. If ƒ′ is also differentiable, then we can differentiate ƒ′ to get a new function of x denoted by ƒ″. So ƒ″ = (ƒ′)′. The function ƒ″ is called the second derivative of ƒ because it is the deriv- ative of the first derivative. It is written in several ways:"},{"x":0.45802,"y":0.82153,"w":0.0787,"h":0.02386,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"ƒ″(x) = d2y"},{"x":0.5612,"y":0.82216,"w":0.04359,"h":0.0305,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"dx ady"},{"x":0.58937,"y":0.82216,"w":0.07127,"h":0.0305,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"dxb = dy′"},{"x":0.51517,"y":0.82538,"w":0.05783,"h":0.02889,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"dx2 = d"},{"x":0.64252,"y":0.83118,"w":0.17629,"h":0.02148,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":0,"t":"dx = y″ = D2(ƒ)(x) = Dx"},{"x":0.81806,"y":0.83118,"w":0.03801,"h":0.01421,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":0,"t":"2ƒ(x)."},{"x":0.36258,"y":0.86187,"w":0.48282,"h":0.01421,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"The symbol D2 means the operation of differentiation is performed twice."},{"x":0.39203,"y":0.87722,"w":0.24815,"h":0.01421,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"If y = x6, then y′ = 6x5 and we have"},{"x":0.56079,"y":0.8981,"w":0.05877,"h":0.02311,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"y″ = dy′"},{"x":0.60144,"y":0.90122,"w":0.05443,"h":0.02728,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"dx = d"},{"x":0.64407,"y":0.90702,"w":0.10975,"h":0.0215,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":0,"t":"dx (6x5) = 30x4."},{"x":0.36258,"y":0.93771,"w":0.14145,"h":0.01421,"fs":0.01401,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"Thus D2(x6) = 30x4."}]}